body:
`ObjectKernel.validateSystemRequirements()` logs a warning for missing core-criticality services but provides no fallback — so `ctx.getService('cache')` crashes in production without Redis. Working Map-backed implementations already exist in `DevPlugin` but are inaccessible to the kernel.

### Changes

- **New `packages/core/src/fallbacks/`** — extracted `createMemoryCache`, `createMemoryQueue`, `createMemoryJob` factories from `plugin-dev`, marked `_fallback: true` instead of `_dev: true`
- **`CORE_FALLBACK_FACTORIES`** — exported map of `{ cache, queue, job }` → factory functions
- **`ObjectKernel.validateSystemRequirements()`** — auto-injects fallback when a core service is missing and a factory exists:

```typescript
} else if (criticality === 'core') {
    const factory = CORE_FALLBACK_FACTORIES[serviceName];
    if (factory) {
        const fallback = factory();
        this.registerService(serviceName, fallback);
        this.logger.warn(`Service '${serviceName}' not provided — using in-memory fallback`);
    } else {
        this.logger.warn(`CORE: Core service missing, functionality may be degraded: ${serviceName}`);
        missingCoreServices.push(serviceName);
    }
}
```

- **`plugin-dev`** — replaced local `createCacheStub`/`createQueueStub`/`createJobStub` with imports from `@objectstack/core`
- **Tests** — 20 new tests covering all three fallback implementations + `CORE_FALLBACK_FACTORIES` shape

No new dependencies. No changes to `@objectstack/spec`.

